<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico drains 546 mln pesos.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico drains 546 mln pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico sold a single lot of Cetes (Treasury Certificates), in its daily intervention in the secondary market, effectively draining 546 million pesos on Tuesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes were sold as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM     AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    546 million    2 days   25.48 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>((--Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
